          %ul
            %li
              commutes with multiplication because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \odot
              preserves composition (similar reasoning),
            %li is compatible with the left unitor by naturality and the coherence laws,
            %li is compatible with the associator by naturality and the coherence laws.
          %h2#on_closed_and_monoidal_closed_categories On closed and monoidal closed categories
          %p
            If the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} monoidal closed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+homs"} internal homs
          %p
            In this section, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\otimes 1)
            be monoidal closed, with internal hom denoted by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit of the hom-tensor adjunction
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_X:X \to [Y,X\otimes Y]
            and the counit (or
            = succeed "," do
              %em evaluation map
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom#EvaluationMap"} internal hom - evaluation map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi Y
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_Y:[X,Y]\otimes X \to Y
          %h3#LeftStrongMonadsAreEnrichedMonads Left-strong monads are enriched monads
          %p
            The original reference for this part is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#kock72"} Kock ‘72
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "enriched+monad#RelationToStrongMonads"} enriched monad – Relation to strong and monoidal monads
          %p
            Beware that
            %a{:href => "#kock72"} Kock ‘72
            uses somewhat different terminology:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The left-strength as defined here is called
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensorial+strength"} tensorial strength
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+monad"} enrichment
                of the monad is called
                = succeed "." do
                  %em strength
          %p
            Since the two notions are equivalent under mild conditions see (
            %a{:href => "enriched+monad#RelationToStrongMonads"}> there
            ), the different terminology does not lead to confusion (once the equivalence is established).
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            First of all, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensorial+strength"} strong endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on a closed monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is “the same thing” as a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched endofunctor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo →
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [X,Y] \;\to\; [T X, T Y]
          %p
            which satisfies the usual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            rules (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/currying"} currying
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo →
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi T
                  %mi Y
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [X,Y] \otimes T X \;\to\; T Y.
          %p
            The latter is provided by the strength
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
