          %p
            One can verify that these assignments are inverse to each other. Moreover, the
            %a{:href => "#ConcreteDefinition"} strength diagrams
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            commute if and only the resulting assigment is indeed an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+monad"} enriched monad
          %h4#example-in-set Example in Set
          %p
            %em
              Every monad on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              is
              = succeed "-enriched." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %p
            Given a monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo →
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [X,Y] \;\to\; [T X, T Y]
          %p
            is just the action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo →
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{Hom}(X,Y) \;\to\; \mathrm{Hom}(T X, T Y) .
          %p
            Under
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/currying"} currying
