          %h3#rightstrength_and_pointwise_structure Right-strength and pointwise structure
          %p
            The reference for this part can be found in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#kock71"} Kock ‘71, Section 1
          %p
            Let’s give a preliminary definition. A
            %em pointwise structure
            or
            %em cotensorial strength
            (
            %a{:href => "#kock72"}> Kock ‘72
            ) of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+category"} closed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  s' _{X,Y}: T[X,Y] \to [X, T Y]
